            <ArticleTitle>Neurocysticercosis: a new differential in the diagnosis of postdural puncture headache.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>580-2, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Positional headache after spinal anesthesia is considered pathognomonic for postdural puncture headache. This report describes a patient who developed a positional headache after spinal anesthesia that was due to neurocysticercosis, a parasitic central nervous system infestation caused by the tapeworm Taenia solium.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
